import sailpoint.connector.webservices.EndPoint;
import java.util.*;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TODO 1: Log the outgoing call.
//   log.debug the method and full URL. Look at what EndPoint exposes:
//   getFullUrl(), getHttpMethodType(), getBody(), getHeader().
//
// TODO 2: Add a correlation header.
//   Get the header Map (requestEndPoint.getHeader()), create it if null,
//   put "X-Request-Id" = UUID.randomUUID().toString(), set it back with
//   requestEndPoint.setHeader(map).
//   Verify: the header won't show in /admin/log (that logs body/query),
//   so log it here and compare against the request time in /admin/log.
//
// TODO 3 (provisioning only): Block privileged grants.
//   If provisioningPlan != null, loop its AccountRequests and their
//   AttributeRequests. If an Add for attribute "roles" has value "R400",
//   throw new Exception("System Admin must be granted through PAM").
//   Verify: request R400 in the sandbox and watch the request fail with
//   your message.
//
// Note: the EndPoint import path differs between connector versions. If
//   import fails, delete that line - BeanShell resolves the type at runtime.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

return requestEndPoint;
